//! `ply run` — one entry point evaluated, what is disclosed about the run before it starts, and
//! what is reported once it is over. The unit is opened, bound and entered through `std.machine`:
//! which entry runs, what the binding is resolved against and discloses, what both forms say and
//! the code the run exits with are decided here.
//!
//! A deployed artifact runs the unit it carries once every part of it agrees, rather than a source
//! tree, so it is a second shape of the same report: the same keys wherever the two agree, the file
//! and its digest where they do not.
//!
//! A run of sources keeps what running it reads of its front end in the memo store, with the library
//! its unit was compiled into, as a function of what its load asked: while nothing that load read
//! moved, a run takes it back and runs no front end at all, and reports the same either way.

